.vscode/
bin/
lib/*.a
var/
*.o
*.d
.DS_Store
/tetrish
.tetrishrc
external/tetriSH
*.log
log
.cache
compile_commands.json
auth/jwt_secret
# SimpleDB test artifacts, written into the repo root by `ant test`
simple*.db

# Fuzzing: libFuzzer's raw crash dumps and llvm-cov's output are per-run and
# machine-local. What IS committed is tests/fuzz/corpus/ (the accumulated
# knowledge of every run) and tests/fuzz/regress/ (minimised crashes, replayed
# by `make fuzz-regress` forever) - a crash worth keeping gets filed there, not
# left in artifacts/.
tests/fuzz/artifacts/
tests/fuzz/cov/
# Fuzzer-discovered corpus inputs.
#
# The SEED corpus (make fuzz-seed) IS committed, and gitignore does not apply
# to already-tracked files, so the seeds keep working normally. This rule only
# hides what a campaign discovers on top: near-random bytes git cannot
# delta-compress, in a set that fuzz-merge rewrites wholesale every run.
# libFuzzer names those files after their SHA1 with no prefix, so there is no
# pattern that matches them and not the seeds - hence ignore-everything, and
# the seeds stay visible by virtue of being tracked. Discovered inputs live in
# the CI cache instead; see .github/workflows/fuzz.yml.
#
# Adding a genuinely new seed by hand therefore needs: git add -f <path>.
tests/fuzz/corpus/*/*

# Coverage counters, dropped wherever an instrumented binary happens to run.
*.profraw
*.profdata
